+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 474a6307ce (crbug 576333024), M156 reland
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 25-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0007`). V8 15.6 474a6307ce
+(15.6.75.84, 25-11; bugs 584997097 and 576333024), the reland of af144bc8d4 (15.6.75.59), which a62636bc52 (15.6.75.60)
+reverted because it "depends on" crbug 566156384 (failure on the m156 `fuchsia-x64-cast-receiver-rel` bot). The reland is
+byte-identical to the original (same `patch-id`). Upstream now ships it in Chrome 156; no commit naming 566156384 shows
+up on branch-heads 8078 or 8154. Applied as is to 15.6.75.66. Severity not published.
+
+- `Builtins::InvokeApiFunction` called C++ `FunctionTemplate` callbacks (from `Execution::Invoke` and from accessor
+  get/set) without the `DisallowJavascriptExecution` / `ThrowOnJavascriptExecution` / `DumpOnJavascriptExecution`
+  checks that `Execution::Invoke` applies to JS. It now applies them, except for side-effect-free API constructor
+  calls (`Function::NewInstanceWithSideEffectType(..., kHasNoSideEffect)`; comment only in `include/v8-function.h`).
+- `ValueDeserializer::ReadJSMap`/`ReadJSSet` fill the `OrderedHashMap`/`OrderedHashSet` directly in C++ instead of
+  calling `Map.prototype.set`/`Set.prototype.add`, so they no longer need an `AllowJavascriptExecution` scope.
+- `src/api/api.cc` already had a FlyWeb patch; the rest are new files in `patches/v8`.
+
+**Risk:** behaviour change. Embedder code (Blink or Brave) that calls an API function inside a no-JS scope now throws
+or, under `DumpOnJavascriptExecution`, crashes the process. Chrome 156 ships it, so the Chromium side is covered; Brave
+code paths need the usual browsing run.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): mjsunit `value-serializer`, `cctest/test-api/*InvokeApi*`, `*NoJS*` and `*DisallowJavascript*`
+tests, `unittests --gtest_filter='ValueSerializerTest.*'`, plus full mjsunit (no new failures).
+
